# PAN (SHAPE's page after TIDES): each voice's place in the field on K1-K4 (DRONE, VOX, PULSE, TEXTURE), and
# ALGO the RATE they sway at: TIDE, or a cycle of its own (60 s .. 0.5 s). Moved while playing, the voices
# glide across without a click. PAN 2: how far each part sways (VOX: its echoes half as far), and its OFFSET
# (all the way: half a cycle between them, so PULSE mirrors DRONE). With a short tide and VOX swaying all the
# way, VOX travels; on a RATE of about a second, it crosses the field in half of one. SEL twice puts each
# page back as made: every voice in the middle on the tide; VOX swaying a quarter of the way. Audio in pan.wav,
# pan2.wav.
wait 500
tap ENV
turn SELECT 8
expect page 8
expect pan0 64
expect pan1 64
expect sway_rate 0
turn K2 -32
expect pan1 0
turn K3 32
expect pan2 127
turn K4 -10
expect pan3 44
turn K1 10
expect pan0 84
shot pan.png
wav pan.wav
tapkey w2
tapkey b6
wait 600
turn K2 32 40
expect pan1 64
tapkey w4
wait 400
turn K1 -40 30
expect pan0 4
turn SELECT -1
expect page 7
turn K1 -40
turn ALGO -40
turn SELECT 2
expect page 9
expect sway1 32
turn K2 50
expect sway1 127
turn SELECT -1
tapkey w3
wait 1500
expect pan_now1 <40
tapkey w5
wait 2000
expect pan_now1 <30
turn ALGO 54
expect sway_rate 108
tapkey w2
wait 250
expect pan_now1 >100
wait 500
expect pan_now1 <25
wait 1500
wavstop
expect clips 0
tap SEL
tap SEL
wait 100
expect pan0 64
expect pan1 64
expect pan3 64
expect sway_rate 0
turn SELECT 1
expect page 9
turn K2 -64
turn K1 64
turn K3 64
expect sway0 127
expect sway1 0
expect sway2 127
turn ALGO 64
expect sway_off 127
wav pan2.wav
tapkey b5
wait 1000
shot pan2.png
expect pan_now0 >64
expect pan_now2 <64
expect pan_now1 64
tapkey b5
wait 2000
expect pan_now0 <10
expect pan_now2 >117
wavstop
expect clips 0
tap SEL
tap SEL
wait 100
expect sway0 0
expect sway1 32
expect sway_off 0
